--TEST--
`Core\Env::mode` and the `mode.default` directive agree after an accepted flip, after a refused one and after a flip back — `rule:config/a-program-may-read-and-flip-its-mode` and `rule:http-server/the-mode-ceiling-defaults-to-the-startup-mode`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Env\Mode
// § 4's flip is a `Core\Config::set` on `mode.default`, and this member reports
// what the flip left in force. So the two are one fact reached two ways, and
// this case asserts they **agree** at every step rather than asserting what
// either one said: a `mode()` that had grown a reader of its own still looks
// right on its own line and fails here.

echo "start=", Core\Config::get("mode.default") ?? "unset", " member=", (Core\Env::mode() == Core\Env\Mode::Production) ? "Production" : "Development", "\n";

// § 5: the ceiling is `development`, so this flip is within it.
echo "flip=", Core\Config::set("mode.default", "development") ? "true" : "false", "\n";
echo "now=", Core\Config::get("mode.default") ?? "unset", " member=", (Core\Env::mode() == Core\Env\Mode::Development) ? "Development" : "Production", "\n";

// A mode nobody defined is outside every ceiling, so the set is refused. The
// half a refusal could quietly leave behind is this member, which must still be
// reading what is in force rather than what was last asked for.
echo "bogus=", Core\Config::set("mode.default", "staging") ? "true" : "false", "\n";
echo "now=", Core\Config::get("mode.default") ?? "unset", " member=", (Core\Env::mode() == Core\Env\Mode::Development) ? "Development" : "Production", "\n";

// And back, because a flip is a set and not a one-way latch.
echo "back=", Core\Config::set("mode.default", "production") ? "true" : "false", "\n";
echo "now=", Core\Config::get("mode.default") ?? "unset", " member=", (Core\Env::mode() == Core\Env\Mode::Production) ? "Production" : "Development", "\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
# § 5's third row: production by default, and a request may select development.
[mode]
default = "production"
ceiling = "development"
--EXPECT--
start=production member=Production
flip=true
now=development member=Development
bogus=false
now=development member=Development
back=true
now=production member=Production
